// Real street-segment data for downtown Chicago, weighted toward the Loop
// itself -- east through Grant Park to Lake Shore Dr and the lake, west only
// as far as Canal St so Union Station stays on the map. Sourced once from the
// City of Chicago open data portal ("Street Center Lines" dataset, Socrata
// resource id pr57-gg9e) on 2026-11-22. Includes every real named street in
// that bounding box -- not just the main arterials -- except expressway ramps,
// interchange connectors, and lower-level duplicates of a street already
// mapped at surface level (e.g. Wacker Lower, Randolph Lower). Bundled here as
// static data -- the app never calls a live API.
//
// The raw dataset breaks a street at every real-world node (including minor
// alleys/courts we do not otherwise track); those sub-block pieces are merged
// here into one segment per block between two of our named cross streets, so
// every clickable unit corresponds to a visible intersection on the map. For
// Columbus Dr and Lake Shore Dr specifically, "named cross streets" also
// includes Grant Park's own signed drives (Balbo, Congress, Jackson, Monroe,
// Roosevelt Dr) even though they are not themselves separately explorable --
// without that, those two streets would merge straight through the whole park.
// Lake Shore Dr is a divided road in the source data (separate northbound/
// southbound carriageways) and is kept here as two parallel streets.
//
// deadEndFrom/deadEndTo: true only when the source data itself tags that end
// a literal dead end (the street really stops there in real life), not when
// it simply runs into an untracked alley or the edge of our mapped area.

